.TH SWAYDESK-CALENDAR 1 2026-11-14 "swaydesk 0.1.10" "Sway desktop components"
.SH NAME
swaydesk\-calendar \- calendar popup for the Waybar clock
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B swaydesk\-calendar
.SH DESCRIPTION
Shows the month in the interface language, today in the accent color, and the holidays of the configured country (through python3\-holidays, when it is installed). The arrows and the scroll wheel change the month; Today goes back. When it opens and closes it sends SIGUSR1 to the Waybar clock, which hides its tooltip.
.PP
Running it again while the popup is open closes it, and opening it closes the other popups of the bar. Esc, clicking outside or switching workspace also closes it.
.PP
The session runs it under the name waybar\-calendar (a link in the package's helper directory to /usr/bin/swaydesk\-calendar); the process name is waybar\-calendar too.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-check
Exit 0 at once without doing anything: the Python launchers use it to check that the binary and its libraries load.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/swaydesk/config.toml
The desktop configuration: language, accent color, GTK and icon themes, folder color, file manager, weather location and holidays.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR swaydesk (7)
